![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

If `gcsFileInfo` is available and we know the file size, we can determine beforehand if the requested range `[position, position + length)` exceeds the file boundary. If it does, `readFully` is guaranteed to throw an `EOFException`.

Currently, the code still opens a new GCS channel (`openReadChannel`), seeks to the position, and attempts to read before throwing the exception. Opening a GCS channel is an expensive network operation. We should fail fast and throw the `EOFException` immediately before opening the channel to avoid unnecessary network I/O.

```java
              if (gcsFileInfo != null && gcsFileInfo.getItemInfo().getSize() >= 0) {
                long size = gcsFileInfo.getItemInfo().getSize();
                if (position + length > size) {
                  throw new EOFException(
                      "Reached the end of stream with "
                          + (position + length - size)
                          + " bytes left to read");
                }
              }
              int bytesToRead = length;
```

